    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Scholars argue that IQ scores and standardized testing are culturally and socioeconomically biased, reflecting existing power dynamics rather than objective ability. Critiques include the concept of \" legitimacy bias\" (Tucker & Oakes, 2007), where high-achieving students from affluent backgrounds receive advantages, while disadvantaged students face systemic barriers. También, implicit bias in tests (Devlin et al., 2006) can influence scores and affect fairness. Standardized testing neglects the role of privilege, socio-economic status, and systemic inequality.",
