      "content": "Scholars argue that the tests are not an objective measure of merit or talent, but rather a selection tool that perpetuates existing social inequalities (A newUser, 2009). They contend that standardized tests, such as the SAT and ACT, are over-emphasized in the college admissions process, neglecting other important factors like creativity, critical thinking, and life experience. Researchers also point out that measuring IQ is an attempt to reconstruct the shape of intelligence to fit an idealized notion of human progress ( Flynn, 2007), which is often a culturally and historically constructed concept. Some argue that the emphasis on these tests serves to reinforce a rigid, utilitarian meritocracy that undervalues diversity, critical thinking, and talent in non-traditional contexts.\n\nPlease let me know if you want more.",
